11
00:47:08,571 --> 00:47:14,571
Rocky is a 1976 American independent sports drama film directed by John G.

12
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
Avildsen, written by and starring Sylvester Stallone.

13
00:55:42,857 --> 00:55:48,857
It is the first installment in the Rocky franchise and also stars Talia
Shire, Burt Young, Carl Weathers, and Burgess Meredith.

14
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
In the film, Rocky Balboa (Stallone), a poor small-time club fighter and loanshark debt collector from Philadelphia, gets
an unlikely once in a lifetime shot at the world heavyweight championship held by Apollo Creed (Weathers).

15
01:04:17,142 --> 01:04:23,142
Rocky entered development in March 1975, after
Stallone wrote the screenplay in three days.

16
01:08:34,285 --> 01:08:40,285
It entered a complicated production process after Stallone refused to allow the film to be made without him in the lead role;
United Artists eventually agreed to cast Stallone after he rejected a six figure deal for the film rights.

17
01:12:51,428 --> 01:12:57,428
Principal photography began in January 1976, with filming primarily held in Philadelphia; several
locations featured in the film, such as the Rocky Steps, are now considered cultural landmarks.

18
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
With an estimated production budget of under $1.1 million, Rocky popularized the rags to
riches and American Dream themes of sports dramas which preceded the film.

19
01:21:25,714 --> 01:21:31,714
Rocky had its premiere in New York City on November 20, 1976, and was
released in the United States on December 3, 1976.

20
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
Rocky became the highest-grossing film of 1976, earning
approximately $225 million worldwide.

21
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The film received critical acclaim for Stallone's writing, as well as the film's performances, direction, musical score, cinematography
and editing; among other accolades, it received ten Academy Award nominations and won three, including Best Picture.

22
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
It has been ranked by numerous publications as one of the greatest films of
all time, as well as one of the most iconic sports films ever.

23
01:38:34,285 --> 01:38:40,285
Rocky and its theme song have become a pop-cultural phenomenon and
an important part of 1970s American popular culture.

24
01:42:51,428 --> 01:42:57,428
In 2006, the Library of Congress selected Rocky for preservation in the United States National
Film Registry as being "culturally, historically or aesthetically significant".

25
01:47:08,571 --> 01:47:14,571
The first sequel in the series, Rocky II, was released in 1979.

26
01:51:25,714 --> 01:51:31,714
The film explores themes of underdog, philadelphia, pennsylvania,
transporter, love of one's life, italian american.

27
01:55:42,857 --> 01:55:48,857
The tone is uplifting and emotional.
